course: dictionary
lesson: 7126
title: The pelvis
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The pelvis is the large ring of bones at the bottom of your spine. It joins your legs to your body, so your hips are part of it. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «Each hip bone looks like one bone but is really three fused together, and together the hips form the pelvis, a bowl that passes your weight down to your legs and shelters organs inside.» The clues are bowl, weight and legs. The pelvis is a bowl-shaped part that carries your weight down into your legs.
explain: «The two hip bones and the base of the spine form the pelvis, which carries the upper body's weight to the legs and protects organs.» This says the same idea in other words. Pelvis is a noun, so you can say one pelvis or two pelvises (or pelves).
fact: The pelvis is a noun: one pelvis, two pelvises or two pelves.
fact: «Pelvis» means the large ring of bones at the bottom of your spine, which joins your legs to your body.
fact: Your hips are part of your pelvis.
fact: The pelvis protects organs in the lower body and holds up the upper body.
fact: Your leg bones, called femurs, fit into the pelvis at the hip joints.
exercise: What is the pelvis? | Your heart and lungs | Muscles in your arm | *The large ring of bones at the bottom of your spine | Your skull, which protects your brain
exercise: «The pelvis passes your weight down to your legs.» What does the pelvis pass your weight down to? | Your arms | *Your legs | Your ribs | Your head
exercise: What does the pelvis protect? | *Organs in the lower body | Your eyes | Your fingernails | Your ears
test: «Your hips are part of the pelvis.» What are your hips part of? | Your lungs | Your fingers | Your head | *Your pelvis
test: In a skeleton, where do the leg bones (femurs) fit? | Into the ribs | *Into the pelvis at the hip joints | Into the skull | Into the arms
exam: Which of these does the pelvis do? | *Holds up the upper body and protects organs | Stores food for winter | Pumps blood round the body | Helps you hear sounds
